<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103963" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῑμαλφ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>do honour to</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. λόγοις νίκαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					9.54
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοὺς τοῖσδε τ. χρεών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					922
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μολόντα τ</span>.
			<i>celebrate</i> any one's arrival, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				15
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκήπτροισι
			τιμαλφούμενος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				626
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπ᾽ ἀστῶν . . τ</span>.
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				807
			</span></i>:— rare in Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. τοὺς θεούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1336b19
				</span></i>
			; and in later Poetry, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. τὰν σὰν . . θυμέλαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Sammelb.</u>
					6699.2
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>:—<i><span class="en">
				Epich.
			</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				214
			</span></i>) ridiculed Aeschylus for his use of this word.</div>
